From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:28:09 -0400
Subject: libclamav: Bound UPX decompression output (#155)

UPX decoder attempts share a destination buffer while passing its
logical content length by pointer. A successful NRV decode can enlarge
that length before the LZMA detector runs a second decoder against the
same allocation, allowing a crafted executable to write beyond the
heap buffer.

Try explicit LZMA stub signatures before heuristic NRV fallbacks and
stop after the first decoded stream. Pass the immutable allocation
capacity through the decoder and PE rebuild paths, validate it before
decoding, and bound rebuilt section copies against both decoded input
and physical destination before allocating the rebuilt image.

Require complete LZMA output, propagate rebuilt image lengths, clear
failed LZMA output before decoder fallback, account for its skipped
source prefix, and decode NRV back-reference offsets without signed
left-shift overflow.

Reported by Feng Xue.

CLAM-3092

